Access Modifiers -
    -access modifiers defines the visibility and the accessibility of the classes and methods
        other members.
    -they determine where these members can be accessed within the code.

Need -
        1.security- restrict unwanted access
        2.encapsulation - hide internal data
        3.controlled access - give access only where required.
        4.clean design - avoid miss use of variables and methods.

types -
        1.Public
        2.Private
        3.Protected
        4.Default

1.Public -
        -accessible from every where means same class, package, different class, method, package

2.Private
        - accessible only same inside class.
        -
3.Protected -
            - accessible in same package as well as different subClasses.

4.Default -
            - accessible only within the same package.